Subject: block rows: a pinned driver's bdevsw rows from its mod_drv_data

30 section 2 patch 7 (S4-06).  The core refused any driver with
drv_bcount; the ramdisk (block major 20) needs a block row.  A driver
may now have consecutive block majors, each registered to it (b: in the
registry), with or without character rows.  The block switch has no
first-open trampoline, so the row is filled when the module links and
only a pinned module may have one.  The row must be empty (every routine
nodev, no flag set), the entries module code or 0 (0 is nodev); a block
row that cannot link puts the driver's character rows back, and a
failed load puts the row back.  The bdevsw layout is measured
(dlmoffs.c: DRV_BDEVSW, DRV_BMAJOR, BD_NFN, BD_FLAG), which is an added
ABI name: the stage-4 kabi minor, k46.1.1 / k30.1.1.

